17	/**
18	 * notify_service.c — Gerrit/Jira polling → LVGL notification page.
19	 *
20	 * Thread model: a single detached notify_thread, cond_timedwait-driven,
21	 * each source keeping its own next-due timestamp.  Polling is a sync
22	 * mcp_client_execute() call on this thread (never on agent_loop).
23	 *
24	 * Dedup: Gerrit polls with a last-updated window (-age:) and keeps a small
25	 * in-memory LRU of the change numbers it reported, so what gets notified is
26	 * "updated since the previous poll" rather than "id larger than everything
27	 * seen".  The id-cursor version could never report a new patch set on an
28	 * existing change — the normal upload path — and replayed the whole
29	 * open-change backlog after a re-flash.  Jira keys are "PROJ-123"
30	 * (non-numeric) → store a last-seen key + a small in-memory LRU.
31	 *
32	 * Cursor persistence: config_store (claw_config_get/set).  Cursor is
33	 * updated in memory first, then pushed to outbound, then persisted — so
34	 * a push failure (message bus full) does NOT lose the cursor (we'd rather
35	 * miss a notification this round and re-report next round than silently
36	 * advance the cursor past something the user never saw).
37	 */
